      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The content of lipid peroxidation products--hydroperoxides with conjugated double bonds and fluorescent compounds, which are formed on interaction of primary lipid peroxidation products and proteins, considerably increases in blood plasma of patients suffering from coronary heart disease. Treatment with combined vitamins E and C enables the blood plasma lipid peroxidation products to be decreased to a far greater extent as compared with conventional therapy."},
